<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schleiz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Schleiz is a small town in the Saale-Orla district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. From the 17th century it was the residence of a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-reuss">House of Reuss</a> Younger Line, whose counts and later princes ruled Reuss-Schleiz from its palace until the lands were united in 1848. The palace was destroyed in 1945. The town is also known for the Schleizer Dreieck, a historic motor-racing circuit.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/schleiz.jpg" alt="Schleiz" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Sander · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stadtkirche_Schleiz.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
